      "content": "The problem is that the memo specifically shows they voted 'Nay' on the exact bill that would have secured the immediate funding. If we just say \"feasibility concerns,\" the press is going to point to the vote and say, \"If you were so concerned about the details, why didn't you just vote for an amendment or a different version? You just killed the project.\" We can't just be vague. Is there a way we can frame the actual vote as being for a different purpose, so it doesn't look like they were just being obstructionist?",
